# The thread dump of debug and test builds (roadmap l4.md L2), on the AT's
# Sys Req key: every thread, its state and priority, and how much of the
# kernel's one stack has been used (roadmap os-server.md P3). The keyboard
# driver asks for the dump (roadmap l4.md L8), and is running; the shell
# waits for the reply of the OS server's thread, which sleeps until the
# keyboard driver signals (roadmap os-server.md P5); the OS server's control
# thread awaits Ctrl+Break; the mouse's
# driver is still in the mouse's reset (roadmap l4.md L7), but on MAME,
# where the drivers, at 7 above the root at 6 (roadmap os-server.md P4),
# have run long enough to finish it.
program: shell
keys: {sysrq}
match: contains
---
rx286: thread root receiving priority 6
rx286: thread printer receiving priority 7
@bochs rx286: thread mouse awaiting a notification priority 7
@mame rx286: thread mouse receiving priority 7
@dosbox-x rx286: thread mouse awaiting a notification priority 7
rx286: thread console receiving priority 7
rx286: thread kbd running priority 7
rx286: thread fd receiving priority 7
rx286: thread hd receiving priority 7
rx286: thread serial receiving priority 7
rx286: thread sound receiving priority 7
rx286: thread rtc receiving priority 7
rx286: thread program awaiting its reply priority 3
rx286: thread counter ready priority 1
rx286: thread os awaiting a notification priority 5
rx286: thread os awaiting a notification priority 5
rx286: thread os receiving priority 5
rx286: the kernel's stack used
